Q24.what is Encapsulation ?
Wrapping of data (encapsulation = data hiding + controlled access to data.)
Encapsulation is an OOP concept that bundles data and methods into a class and restricts direct access to the data using access modifiers like private, while providing controlled access through methods or properties.

Q25 . what is Abstraction 
“Abstract class ही अशी class आहे जिचा object आपण create करू शकत नाही. ती multiple child classes मध्ये common functionality देण्यासाठी वापरली जाते आणि abstract methods च्या माध्यमातून child classes ना specific functionality implement करणे compulsory करते.”
•	Abstract class मध्ये fields, properties आणि normal methods असू शकतात. 
•	Abstract method मध्ये implementation नसते. 
•	Child class ने abstract method compulsory override करावी लागते. 
•	Abstract class चा object create करता येत नाही. 
Abstraction means hiding unnecessary implementation details and showing only the essential features to the user.
An abstract class is a class that cannot be instantiated, meaning we cannot create an object of it. It is used to provide common functionality to child classes and to force child classes to implement specific functionality using abstract methods.
Key Points
•	❌ Cannot create an object of an abstract class. 
•	✅ Can contain fields, properties, and normal methods. 
•	✅ Can contain abstract methods without implementation. 
•	✅ Child classes must override abstract methods. 
•	✅ Used when multiple child classes share common functionality.


