What is process?
a program is  under execution it call process.

What is a Thread?
A thread is a small unit of execution inside a program. It allows a program to perform a task independently or concurrently.

What is Multithreading ?
Multithreading is a technique of executing multiple threads concurrently within a process. It is mainly used to handle multiple tasks efficiently and improve application responsiveness.
Why use Multithreading?
•	Perform multiple tasks concurrently 
•	Improve application responsiveness 
•	Useful for I/O-bound tasks like API calls, file operations, and database operations




What is Multiprocessing?
Multiprocessing is a technique where a program uses multiple processes to perform tasks independently.Each process has its own memory space and can run on a separate CPU core.
Why use Multiprocessing?
Mainly for CPU-bound tasks, such as:
•	Large calculations 
•	Image/video processing 
•	Data processing 
•	Machine learning computations
Import the module use it manully
What is Thread Pool?
A Thread Pool is a collection of reusable threads. When a task comes, it uses an available thread from the pool, and after completing the task, the thread becomes available for another task.
Why use Thread Pool?
•	Avoid creating new threads again and again 
•	Reuse threads 
•	Better performance 
•	Manage many tasks efficiently 

What is Synchronous Programming?
Synchronous programming means tasks are executed one after another. The next task starts only after the current task is completed.

What is Asynchronous programming
Asynchronous programming allows a program to perform other work while waiting for a long-running I/O operation, without blocking the thread. It is commonly used for API calls, database operations, file operations, and network requests

Await keyword
await pauses the current method while an asynchronous operation is running. It does not block the thread, so the thread can do other work. When the operation is completed, an available thread from the thread pool can continue the remaining part of the method.




What is GIL?
GIL stands for Global Interpreter Lock. In CPython, it allows only one thread at a time to execute Python bytecode in a process.
Why is GIL used?
The GIL helps CPython safely manage memory and Python objects.

What is Socket Programming  ?
“Socket Programming is a way of establishing communication between two devices or applications over a network using sockets. It allows the client and server to send and receive data.”
Simple example:
In a chat application, the client and server use sockets to send and receive messages.

What is IP(Internet Protocol)
“An IP address is a unique address assigned to a device on a network. It is used to identify the device and enable communication between devices.”


What is Transmission Control Protocol (TCP)
TCP मध्ये communication सुरू करण्यापूर्वी client आणि server यांच्यामध्ये connection establish होते. त्यामुळे data व्यवस्थित आणि योग्य क्रमाने पोहोचवण्याची खात्री TCP करते.
“A TCP server is a server that uses the TCP protocol to establish a reliable connection with clients and send or receive data over a network.”

What is UDP
“TCP is a connection-oriented and reliable protocol that ensures data is delivered correctly and in order. UDP is a connectionless protocol that is faster but does not guarantee delivery or order of data.”
TCP = Reliable पण थोडे slow
UDP = Fast पण delivery guarantee नाही


