Q. What is an Attribute in C#?
An attribute in C# is a declarative feature used to add metadata to program elements such as classes, methods, and properties. Attributes provide additional information to the compiler or runtime. We can use built-in attributes or create custom attributes by inheriting from the Attribute class.
What is a Property in C#?
A Property in C# is a class member used to access (get) and modify (set) the values of private fields.
Properties provide controlled access to class data and support encapsulation.

What is State in C#?
State refers to the current values of an object's properties or fields at a particular point in time.
In simple words, state represents the current condition or data of an object.
public class Student
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; }
    public int Age { get; set; }
}

Student student = new Student();

student.Id = 101;
student.Name = "Rahul";
student.Age = 23;

Here, the object's state is:
•	Id = 101
•	Name = Rahul
•	Age = 23





Q. What are Class Members in C#?
Class members are the elements declared inside a class. They define the data and behavior of objects. Examples include fields, properties, methods, constructors, events, and indexers.
Class members are divided into two main categories:
1.	Data Members
2.	Function Members

What is a Data Member in C#?
A Data Member is a variable declared inside a class that stores information about an object.
Data members represent the state (data) of an object.

1. Example
public class Student
{
    // Data Members
    public int Id;
    public string Name;
    public int Age;
}
Function members ?
is define the actions or operations that a class can perform. They represent the behavior of an object.
Examples:
•	Methods
•	Constructors
•	Destructors
•	Properties (get/set accessors)
•	Events
•	Indexers
•	Operators

Q1. What is the Waterfall Model?
The Waterfall Model is a traditional Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) model in which software development is completed step by step in a sequential manner.
Each phase must be completed before moving to the next phase. Going back to previous phases is difficult.
1. Phases of Waterfall Model
1.	Requirement Analysis: Collect and understand customer requirements.
2.	System Design: Design the software architecture and database.
3.	Implementation: Developers write the code.
4.	Testing: Test the application and identify bugs.
5.	Deployment: Deliver the application to the customer.
6.	Maintenance: Fix bugs and make necessary updates.









Q. What is Agile?
Agile is a software development approach that focuses on iterative development, teamwork, continuous feedback, and flexibility. It divides a large project into smaller tasks and delivers working software incrementally.
What is Iterative Development?
Iterative Development is a software development approach in which an application is developed in small repeated cycles. Each cycle includes development, testing, feedback, and improvement until the final product is completed.
Simple meaning: Build a small part → Test it → Improve it → Repeat.

Q2. What is Scrum?
Scrum is an Agile framework used to manage work and organize tasks among team members using short iterations called Sprints. It helps the team collaborate, track progress, and deliver work regularly.
•	Agile = Software development approach.
•	Scrum = Agile framework.
•	Sprint = Fixed time period for completing work.
•	Product Backlog = List of all required features.
•	Daily Scrum = Short daily team meeting.




Q5. What is the difference between Scrum and Kanban?
Scrum is an Agile framework used to manage and organize work among team members through fixed time periods called Sprints.
Kanban is an Agile method used to visualize, manage, and track tasks through a visual board. It helps team members understand task status and project progress.
Q. What is Hybrid Methodology?
Hybrid Methodology is a project management approach that combines two or more methodologies, such as Waterfall and Agile. It uses Waterfall for structured planning and Agile for flexible and iterative development. It helps teams manage projects effectively while adapting to changing requirements.

Q..What is framework?
A framework is a predefined software structure that provides reusable code, libraries, tools, and guidelines to develop applications efficiently. It reduces repetitive coding and provides a standard structure for application development.

Q…What is cloud ?
Suppose we want to make our application live in a production environment and available 24/7.
it not possible keeping our local computer running all the time, then we rent a cloud server from a cloud provider like AWS or Azure.
The cloud provider provides infrastructure such as:
•	CPU
•	RAM
•	Storage (Hard Disk)
•	Networking
•	Database services
We deploy our application on that cloud infrastructure.
The cloud provider maintains the infrastructure, and users can access our application through the internet 24/7.
In return, we pay charges based on the resources and services we use.

Q..What is public Cloud ?
Public Cloud is a cloud computing model in which computing resources, such as servers, storage, and networking, are provided over the internet by a third-party cloud provider and shared among multiple customers.
Examples include AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud.

Q..Traditional Data Center vs Cloud 
In a traditional data center, a company buys, installs, and maintains its own physical infrastructure, such as servers, storage, and networking equipment.
In cloud computing, a company rents computing resources from a cloud provider over the internet instead of buying and maintaining its own physical hardware.
1. Traditional Data Center 🖥️
Company स्वतःचा infrastructure arrange करते:
•	CPU / Servers 
•	RAM 
•	Storage 
•	Networking 
•	Power and Cooling 
Company स्वतः hardware खरेदी करते आणि maintain करते.
2. Cloud ☁️
Cloud provider आपल्याला infrastructure उपलब्ध करून देतो:
•	Virtual Servers 
•	CPU and RAM 
•	Storage 
•	Networking 
आपण cloud provider कडून गरजेनुसार resources rent करतो.
AWS, Microsoft Azure आणि Google Cloud ही examples आहेत.


Q..Virtual Machine
Q. What is a Virtual Machine (VM)?
Answer:
A Virtual Machine (VM) is a software-based computer that behaves like a physical computer. It runs an operating system and applications using the resources of a physical machine.
It provides virtual resources such as CPU, RAM, storage, and networking.
In simple words, a Virtual Machine is a computer inside another computer.
1. How Does a Virtual Machine Work?
Suppose you have one physical computer.
You can create multiple Virtual Machines on that computer.
For example:
•	VM 1 → Windows OS
•	VM 2 → Linux OS
•	VM 3 → Ubuntu OS
Each VM works like an independent computer with its own operating system and allocated resources.
3. Virtual Machine in Cloud Computing
Cloud providers like AWS and Azure allow us to rent Virtual Machines.
For example:
•	AWS EC2
•	Azure Virtual Machines
•	Google Compute Engine
You can select:
•	CPU
•	RAM
•	Storage
•	Operating System
Then deploy your application on that VM.
4. Advantages of Virtual Machines
1.	Run multiple operating systems on one physical machine.
2.	Reduce hardware costs.
3.	Easy to create and manage.
4.	Isolate different environments.
5.	Increase or decrease allocated resources.
.

Q what s Devops?
DevOps is a combination of Development (Dev) and Operations (Ops)
DevOps focuses on automation, collaboration, and continuous delivery.

